=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since statement I is true, we have ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ for ${x}_{1}=6,\\,{x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=1.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is false, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275387 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119924 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb5ca50-e9f3-5513-aff1-1ada8c225a42" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent Sets by Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f8fd2e6-05d0-5b30-963b-06e825131288" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449774} {:answer/id #uuid "39c69830-c567-5230-b180-445b08558fce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f8fd2e6-05d0-5b30-963b-06e825131288" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449774} :answer-field/id #uuid "679e9945-ad45-5f9f-bee3-cbf1a39c8865" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450841} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65d6efaa-9a84-5e8e-b314-cdea60127cb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449776} {:answer/id #uuid "af932fb4-f3a2-5971-aec5-9759d804797b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af932fb4-f3a2-5971-aec5-9759d804797b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449777} :answer-field/id #uuid "841e39ca-c1bb-52f0-b7a2-17fd3182feb7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450842} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51338bd6-bb62-534d-8de6-e496d10b0226" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449778} {:answer/id #uuid "51453a9c-1b51-56c2-8aa2-856e4ff4a566" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449779}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51453a9c-1b51-56c2-8aa2-856e4ff4a566" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449779} :answer-field/id #uuid "a474f929-5eb8-5ab7-8b0e-320d9f1b2424" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f4d0dbc3-088e-54a3-8420-9efcf1fc89b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-157253" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $-{a}_{1}+3{a}_{2}=0.$\n- **II.** ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n- **III.** The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly independent." :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{a}_{1}+3{a}_{2} & =-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system using back substitution, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275388 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119924 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb5ca50-e9f3-5513-aff1-1ada8c225a42" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent Sets by Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55ecca7e-205c-5e10-bf65-d3d1bbcd33f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449780} {:answer/id #uuid "35967e25-346a-5de9-bfb8-8a3dc6109d00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449781}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35967e25-346a-5de9-bfb8-8a3dc6109d00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449781} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fc873fa-b153-5bb8-a05a-68748c9b661d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450844} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9ec9533-e9bc-5548-9ecf-a8025a2dbd0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449782} {:answer/id #uuid "39cfb179-6954-589e-b4f1-69e06c027325" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9ec9533-e9bc-5548-9ecf-a8025a2dbd0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449782} :answer-field/id #uuid "371913d2-a95b-5a3b-9671-f48a5aa60350" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450845} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b8eeb26-a33b-5553-b0a8-96e77926df4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449784} {:answer/id #uuid "1fbb17c6-439b-53d6-a2ae-4437ffe7bbea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b8eeb26-a33b-5553-b0a8-96e77926df4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449784} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0e97e6c-fbd7-5c99-8889-ecf8600edbdf" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2e89e99e-07af-5529-a0c3-3af7fe4158cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-157256" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $4{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=0.$\n- **II.** ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n- **III.** The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly independent." :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =4[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}=4{x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275397 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119928 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f3018fd-9d16-578f-b050-966890844c9b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Plane Is a Subspace of Three-Dimensional Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98fdad6c-bf29-53b5-8c45-6b7cb4fe8703" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449786} {:answer/id #uuid "d319819e-c3e4-5493-bd8e-415384a14552" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98fdad6c-bf29-53b5-8c45-6b7cb4f